  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Planets <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> orbit the same star.</p>\n<p>The orbital radius of planet <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R_{X}\"></span>, and that of planet <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R_{Y}\"></span>. The orbital period of planet <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T_{X}\"></span>, and that of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T_{Y}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{T_{Y}}{T_{X}}\"></span>?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R_{Y}}{R_{X}}^{\\frac{3}{2}}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R_{X}}{R_{Y}}^{\\frac{3}{2}}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R_{Y}}{R_{X}}^{\\frac{2}{3}}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R_{X}}{R_{Y}}^{\\frac{2}{3}}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
